  <section id="best-for">
    <h2>Who Kidani Village is best for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Families who want a savanna view and a kitchen,</strong> and will pay more for Savanna View than for a Resort View that looks at the pool or parking.</li>
      <li><strong>People who want table-service dining in the same building.</strong> Sanaa is in Kidani Village, with animal views from some seats.</li>
      <li><strong>Groups who will use Samawati Springs and Uwanja Camp,</strong> especially with younger children who fit the playground's age notes.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Think twice if…</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You need a fifth bed in a studio.</strong> Official 2026 listings cap Deluxe Studios at four adults.</li>
      <li><strong>A short ride to Magic Kingdom or EPCOT is the main reason you're booking Deluxe.</strong> This resort is buses only.</li>
      <li><strong>You assumed a Resort View still included animals.</strong> Official text describes Resort View studios as looking at the pool or parking, and Resort View one-bedrooms as looking at parking.</li>
    </ul>
